                    NSC 34/2, same title, February 28, 1949, are printed in <ref
                        target="frus1949v09#pg_474">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., 1949, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ix</hi>, pp. 474</ref> and <ref target="frus1949v09#pg_474">491</ref>,
                    respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d12-f8" n="8" xml:id="d12-f8-content">
                <p>Documents NSC 37 through 37/9, which were devoted to U.S. policy regarding
                    Formosa, are printed in <ref target="frus1949v09#pg_261">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., pp. 261</ref> ff. NSC 37/10, same
                    subject, August 3, 1950, is printed in <ref target="frus1950v06#pg_413">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., 1950, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >vi</hi>, p. 413</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d12-f9" n="9" xml:id="d12-f9-content">
                <p> NSC 60/1, a report titled “Japanese Peace Treaty,” September 8, 1950, is printed
                    in <ref target="frus1950v06#pg_1293">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., p. 1293</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d12-f10" n="10" xml:id="d12-f10-content">
                <p> NSC 81, a report titled “U.S. Courses of Action With Respect to Korea,”
                    September 1, 1950; NSC 81/1, same title, September 9, 1950; and NSC 81/2, same
                    title, November 14, 1950, are printed in <ref target="frus1950v07#pg_685">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., <hi rendition="#small-caps">vii</hi>,
                        pp. 685</ref>, <ref target="frus1950v07#pg_712">712</ref>, and <ref
                        target="frus1950v07#pg_1150">1150</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d12-f11" n="11" xml:id="d12-f11-content">
                <p> NSC 101, titled “Courses of Action Relative to Communist China and Korea,”
